  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-intro",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": -40,
      "y": -420,
      "init": {
        "label": "Mail merge",
        "body": "# One letter per person\n\nA **Note** is the letter template: its `{{ tags }}` stay literal on the card, and its frontmatter (subject, treasurer) fills in as defaults.\n\nWire it into a **Report**'s **Template** socket and the tags become the report's inputs. Wire the ledger into **Rows** and the report renders one page per row, with `row` and `index` in scope; the page name (`{{ record.Name }}`) names each note.\n\n**Write to Obsidian** then writes one note per page: arm it and press Run.",
        "color": "amber",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 190
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": -40,
      "y": -160,
      "init": {
        "label": "Trip ledger",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\": \"Name\", \"type\": \"string\", \"values\": [\"Ada\", \"Bob\", \"Cy\", \"Dee\"]}, {\"name\": \"Paid\", \"type\": \"number\", \"values\": [120, 40, 0, 80]}, {\"name\": \"Email\", \"type\": \"string\", \"values\": [\"ada@example.com\", \"bob@example.com\", \"cy@example.com\", \"dee@example.com\"]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "paid",
      "type": "GetColumnNode",
      "x": 330,
      "y": -160,
      "init": {
        "label": "Paid column"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "name": "Paid"
      }
    },
    {
